This licence covers the Mr. Zaki Studio software in this repository: its source code and
the apps built from it ("the Studio"). It does not cover the folder `standard/` (see 4).

1. Using the Studio
   You may download, install and use the released Studio, free of charge, for any
   purpose, including commercial use. For example, a school or a learning centre may use
   it to make curricula for its own students.

2. What you make is yours
   The curriculum files (bundles) and other material you make with the Studio belong to
   you. This licence claims no rights in them.

3. Reading the source
   You may read the source code in this repository. You may build it on your own computer
   to check that a released Studio matches it.

   Unless you have the copyright holder's written permission, you may not:
   a. copy, modify, translate or adapt the source code or the Studio, in whole or in part,
      except as needed for the building in 3;
   b. publish, distribute, sell, rent or sublicense the source code, the Studio or a
      changed version of either;
   c. use any part of the source code in another product or service.

4. The bundle standard
   The folder `standard/` has its own licences. Its text is licensed under CC BY 4.0 (see
   `standard/LICENSE-TEXT`). Its JSON Schema and examples are licensed under MIT (see
   `standard/LICENSE-SCHEMA`). This licence does not limit them.

5. Other people's software
   The Studio includes software by others, such as Electron, React, pdf.js, mammoth and
   Tesseract with its language data. That software keeps its own licence, listed in
